{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794559111432,"sessionID":"ses_e2bf334aeffeqJnMnu3uN7SVdV","part":{"partID":"prt_1d40ed7b4002xPP8mXOaKFbSW1","sessionID":"ses_e2bf334aeffeqJnMnu3uN7SVdV","messageID":"msg_1d40eb9f70010gXA238I55LPO1","type":"tool","id":"call_4e9db63ff06b48cab883c412","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs","oldString":"// A dispatched worker's marker makes a CLI answer as a child session, and a child\n// session is not the chat start an arm measures. The rest of the environment stays,\n// so each CLI finds its own home, account and route.\n//\n// The network credentials are the exception, because a turn that reaches a forge\n// with the operator's identity is a side effect no transcript can undo. The token\n// variables go, the GitHub CLI is pointed at an empty folder beside the run log\n// rather than the operator's authenticated one, and an empty credential helper\n// replaces whatever a global git config would have offered. A missing credential\n// then fails at once instead of waiting on a terminal nobody is sitting at.\nconst GITHUB_TOKEN_VARS = Object.freeze(['GH_TOKEN', 'GITHUB_TOKEN', 'GH_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN']);","newString":"// A turn runs with bypassed permissions, so it gets only what a runtime needs to\n// start and authenticate, and every other credential in the operator's shell stays\n// out. The shell basics and each runtime's own prefixes are enough for a CLI to\n// find its home, account and route, while a dispatched worker's marker is not\n// passed at all, because a CLI that answers as a child session is not the chat\n// start an arm measures.\n//\n// The network credentials stay out of the allowlist for the same reason: a turn\n// that reaches a forge with the operator's identity is a side effect no transcript\n// can undo. The GitHub CLI is pointed at an empty folder beside the run log rather\n// than the operator's authenticated one, and an empty credential helper replaces\n// whatever a global git config would have offered. A missing credential then fails\n// at once instead of waiting on a terminal nobody is sitting at.\nconst CHILD_ENV_NAMES = Object.freeze([\n  'PATH',\n  'HOME',\n  'USER',\n  'LOGNAME',\n  'SHELL',\n  'TMPDIR',\n  'TMP',\n  'TEMP',\n  'LANG',\n  'TERM',\n  'TERM_PROGRAM',\n  'COLORTERM',\n  'NO_COLOR',\n]);\n\nconst CHILD_ENV_PREFIXES = Object.freeze([\n  'LC_',\n  'XDG_',\n  'ANTHROPIC_',\n  'CLAUDE_',\n  'CODEX_',\n  'OPENAI_',\n  'OPENCODE_',\n  'LLMGATEWAY_',\n  'PI_',\n  'DEVIN_',\n  'DSH_',\n  'DEEPSEEK_',\n  'OLLAMA_',\n  'SPECKIT_',\n  'SKILL_ADVISOR_',\n  'SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_',\n  'MK_',\n]);"},"output":"Edited .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs","patch":"Index: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs\n===================================================================\n--- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs\n+++ .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs\n@@ -754,20 +754,57 @@\n // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n // One turn\n // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n \n-// A dispatched worker's marker makes a CLI answer as a child session, and a child\n-// session is not the chat start an arm measures. The rest of the environment stays,\n-// so each CLI finds its own home, account and route.\n+// A turn runs with bypassed permissions, so it gets only what a runtime needs to\n+// start and authenticate, and every other credential in the operator's shell stays\n+// out. The shell basics and each runtime's own prefixes are enough for a CLI to\n+// find its home, account and route, while a dispatched worker's marker is not\n+// passed at all, because a CLI that answers as a child session is not the chat\n+// start an arm measures.\n //\n-// The network credentials are the exception, because a turn that reaches a forge\n-// with the operator's identity is a side effect no transcript can undo. The token\n-// variables go, the GitHub CLI is pointed at an empty folder beside the run log\n-// rather than the operator's authenticated one, and an empty credential helper\n-// replaces whatever a global git config would have offered. A missing credential\n-// then fails at once instead of waiting on a terminal nobody is sitting at.\n-const GITHUB_TOKEN_VARS = Object.freeze(['GH_TOKEN', 'GITHUB_TOKEN', 'GH_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN']);\n+// The network credentials stay out of the allowlist for the same reason: a turn\n+// that reaches a forge with the operator's identity is a side effect no transcript\n+// can undo. The GitHub CLI is pointed at an empty folder beside the run log rather\n+// than the operator's authenticated one, and an empty credential helper replaces\n+// whatever a global git config would have offered. A missing credential then fails\n+// at once instead of waiting on a terminal nobody is sitting at.\n+const CHILD_ENV_NAMES = Object.freeze([\n+  'PATH',\n+  'HOME',\n+  'USER',\n+  'LOGNAME',\n+  'SHELL',\n+  'TMPDIR',\n+  'TMP',\n+  'TEMP',\n+  'LANG',\n+  'TERM',\n+  'TERM_PROGRAM',\n+  'COLORTERM',\n+  'NO_COLOR',\n+]);\n \n+const CHILD_ENV_PREFIXES = Object.freeze([\n+  'LC_',\n+  'XDG_',\n+  'ANTHROPIC_',\n+  'CLAUDE_',\n+  'CODEX_',\n+  'OPENAI_',\n+  'OPENCODE_',\n+  'LLMGATEWAY_',\n+  'PI_',\n+  'DEVIN_',\n+  'DSH_',\n+  'DEEPSEEK_',\n+  'OLLAMA_',\n+  'SPECKIT_',\n+  'SKILL_ADVISOR_',\n+  'SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_',\n+  'MK_',\n+]);\n+\n const GIT_CREDENTIAL_OVERRIDES = Object.freeze({\n   GIT_CONFIG_COUNT: '1',\n   GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0: 'credential.helper',\n   GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0: '',\n","status":"modified","additions":47,"deletions":10}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs\",\"oldString\":\"// A dispatched worker's marker makes a CLI answer as a child session, and a child\\n// session is not the chat start an arm measures. The rest of the environment stays,\\n// so each CLI finds its own home, account and route.\\n//\\n// The network credentials are the exception, because a turn that reaches a forge\\n// with the operator's identity is a side effect no transcript can undo. The token\\n// variables go, the GitHub CLI is pointed at an empty folder beside the run log\\n// rather than the operator's authenticated one, and an empty credential helper\\n// replaces whatever a global git config would have offered. A missing credential\\n// then fails at once instead of waiting on a terminal nobody is sitting at.\\nconst GITHUB_TOKEN_VARS = Object.freeze(['GH_TOKEN', 'GITHUB_TOKEN', 'GH_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN']);\",\"newString\":\"// A turn runs with bypassed permissions, so it gets only what a runtime needs to\\n// start and authenticate, and every other credential in the operator's shell stays\\n// out. The shell basics and each runtime's own prefixes are enough for a CLI to\\n// find its home, account and route, while a dispatched worker's marker is not\\n// passed at all, because a CLI that answers as a child session is not the chat\\n// start an arm measures.\\n//\\n// The network credentials stay out of the allowlist for the same reason: a turn\\n// that reaches a forge with the operator's identity is a side effect no transcript\\n// can undo. The GitHub CLI is pointed at an empty folder beside the run log rather\\n// than the operator's authenticated one, and an empty credential helper replaces\\n// whatever a global git config would have offered. A missing credential then fails\\n// at once instead of waiting on a terminal nobody is sitting at.\\nconst CHILD_ENV_NAMES = Object.freeze([\\n  'PATH',\\n  'HOME',\\n  'USER',\\n  'LOGNAME',\\n  'SHELL',\\n  'TMPDIR',\\n  'TMP',\\n  'TEMP',\\n  'LANG',\\n  'TERM',\\n  'TERM_PROGRAM',\\n  'COLORTERM',\\n  'NO_COLOR',\\n]);\\n\\nconst CHILD_ENV_PREFIXES = Object.freeze([\\n  'LC_',\\n  'XDG_',\\n  'ANTHROPIC_',\\n  'CLAUDE_',\\n  'CODEX_',\\n  'OPENAI_',\\n  'OPENCODE_',\\n  'LLMGATEWAY_',\\n  'PI_',\\n  'DEVIN_',\\n  'DSH_',\\n  'DEEPSEEK_',\\n  'OLLAMA_',\\n  'SPECKIT_',\\n  'SKILL_ADVISOR_',\\n  'SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_',\\n  'MK_',\\n]);\"}"},"time":{"start":1794559104948,"end":1794559111432}}}}
